.googleusercontent.com cite78†Image†lh3.googleusercontent.com L239: \nL240: ### Accelerating the frontiers of scientific discovery: Google’s $40M commitment to the Genesis Mission\nL241: \nL242: July 2026\nL243: \nL244: cite79†Learn more†cloud.google.com L245: \nL246: cite80†Image†lh3.googleusercontent.com L247: ### Introducing Gemini 3.5 Flash Cyber\nL248: \nL249: July 2026 Models\nL250: \nL251: cite81†Learn more L252: \nL253: cite82†Image†lh3.googleusercontent.com cite83†Image†lh3.googleusercontent.com L254: \nL255: ### Introducing Gemini 3.6 Flash, 3.5 Flash-Lite, and 3.5 Flash Cyber\nL256: \nL257: July 2026 Models\nL258: \nL259: cite84†Learn more†blog.google L260: \nL261: cite85†Image†lh3.googleusercontent.com cite86†Image†lh3.googleusercontent.com L262: \nL263: ### Our approach to bioresilience\nL264: \nL265: July 2026 Responsibility & Safety\nL266: \nL267: cite87†Learn more L268: \nL269: cite88†Image†lh3.googleusercontent.com --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRelease notes  |  Gemini API  |  Google AI for Developers (https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/changelog)\nciteturn660view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn659view3\",\"pattern\":\"September\"}); Total lines: 943\nL110: The existing `gemini-omni-flash-preview` endpoint will be deprecated on September 30, 2026.\nL111: \nL112: To get started, see the cite11†Gemini Omni Flash model page and the cite12†omni guide .\nL480: ## September 25, 2025\nL481: \nL482:   * Released Gemini Robotics ER 1.5 model in preview. See the cite17†Robotics overview to learn about how to use the model for your robotics application.\nL483: \nL484:   * Launched following preview models:\nL485: \nL486:     * `gemini-2.5-flash-preview-09-2025`\nL487:     * `gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-09-2025`\nL488: \nL489: See the cite83†Models page for details.\nL490: ## September 23, 2025\nL491: \nL492:   * Released `gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-09-2025`, a new native audio model for the Live API with improved function calling and speech cut off handling. To learn more, see the cite73†Live API guide and cite84†Gemini 2.5 Flash Native Audio .\nL493: ## September 16, 2025\nL494: \nL495:   * Deprecation announcement: The following models will be shut down in October 2025:\nL496: \nL497:     * `embedding-001`\nL498:     * `embedding-gecko-001`\nL499:     * `gemini-embedding-exp-03-07` (`gemini-embedding-exp`)\nL500: \nL501: See the cite43†Embeddings page for details on the latest embeddings model.\nL502: \nL503: ## September 10, 2025\nL504: \nL505:   * Released support for the cite85†Embeddings model in Batch API , and added Batch API to the cite86†OpenAI compatibility library for even easier ways to get started with batch queries.\nL506: ## September 9, 2025\nL507: \nL508:   * Launched Veo 3 and Veo 3 Fast GA, with lower pricing and new options for aspect ratios, resolution, and seeding. Read the cite87†Veo documentation for more information.\nL509: \nL510: ## August 26, 2025\nL511: \nL512:   * Launched cite88†Gemini 2.5 Image Preview , our latest native image generation model.\nL727: ## November 21, 2024\nL728: \nL729: Model updates:\nL730: \nL731:   * Released `gemini-exp-1121`, an even more powerful experimental Gemini API model.\nL732: \nL733: Model updates:\nL734: \nL735:   * Updated the `gemini-1.5-flash-latest` and `gemini-1.5-flash` model aliases to use `gemini-1.5-flash-002`.\nL736:     * Change to `top_k` parameter: The `gemini-1.5-flash-002` model supports `top_k` values between 1 and 41 (exclusive). Values greater than 40 will be changed to 40.\nL737: ## November 14, 2024\nL738: \nL739: Model updates:\nL740: \nL741:   * Released `gemini-exp-1114`, a powerful experimental Gemini API model.\nL742: \nL743: ## November 8, 2024\nL744: \nL745: API updates:\nL746: \nL747:   * Added cite122†support for Gemini in the OpenAI libraries / REST API.\nL748: \nL749: ## October 31, 2024\nL750: \nL751: API updates:\nL752: \nL753:   * Added cite102†support for Grounding with Google Search .\nL754: \nL755: ## October 3, 2024\nL756: \nL757: Model updates:\nL758: \nL759:   * Released `gemini-1.5-flash-8b-001`, a stable version of our smallest Gemini API model.\nL760: ## September 24, 2024\nL761: \nL762: Model updates:\nL763:   * Released `gemini-1.5-pro-002` and `gemini-1.5-flash-002`, two new stable versions of Gemini 1.5 Pro and 1.5 Flash, for general availability.\nL764:   * Updated the `gemini-1.5-pro-latest` model code to use `gemini-1.5-pro-002` and the `gemini-1.5-flash-latest` model code to use `gemini-1.5-flash-002`.\nL765:   * Released `gemini-1.5-flash-8b-exp-0924` to replace `gemini-1.5-flash-8b-exp-0827`.\nL766:   * Released the cite129†civic integrity safety filter for the Gemini API and AI Studio.\nL767:   * Released support for two new parameters for Gemini 1.5 Pro and 1.5 Flash in Python and NodeJS: cite130†`frequencyPenalty` and cite131†`presencePenalty` .\nL768: ## September 19, 2024\nL769: \nL770: AI Studio updates:\nL771: \nL772:   * Added thumb-up and thumb-down buttons to model responses, to enable users to provide feedback on the quality of a response.\nL773: \nL774: API updates:\nL775: \nL776:   * Added support for Google Cloud credits, which can now be used towards Gemini API usage.\nL777: ## September 17, 2024\nL778: \nL779: AI Studio updates:\nL780: \nL781:   * Added an Open in Colab button that exports a prompt – and the code to run it – to a Colab notebook. The feature doesn't yet support prompting with tools (JSON mode, function calling, or code execution).\nL782: \nL783: ## September 13, 2024\nL784: \nL785: AI Studio updates:\nL786: \nL787:   * Added support for compare mode, which lets you compare responses across models and prompts to find the best fit for your use case.\nL788: ## August 30, 2024\nL789: \nL790: Model updates:\nL791: \nL792:   * Gemini 1.5 Flash supports cite132†supplying JSON schema through model configuration .\nL793: \nL794: ## August 27, 2024\nL795: \nL796: Model updates:\nL797: \nL798:   * Released the following cite118†experimental models :\nL799:     * `gemini-1.5-pro-exp-0827`\nL800:     * `gemini-1.5-flash-exp-0827`\nL801:     * `gemini-1.5-flash-8b-exp-0827`\nL802: \nL803: ## August 9, 2024\nL804: \nL805: API updates:\nL806: \nL807:   * Added support for cite133†PDF processing .\nL808: \nL809: ## August 5, 2024\nL810: \nL811: Model updates:\nL812: \nL813:   * Fine-tuning support released for Gemini 1.5 Flash.\nL814: ## August 1, 2024\nL815: \nL816: Model updates:\nL817: \nL818:   * Released `gemini-1.5-pro-exp-0801`, a new experimental version of cite134†Gemini 1.5 Pro .\nL819: \nL820: ## July 12, 2024\nL821: \nL822: Model updates:\nL823: \nL824:   * Support for Gemini 1.0 Pro Vision removed from Google AI services and tools.\nL825: \nL826: ## June 27, 2024\nL827: \nL828: Model updates:\nL829: \nL830:   * General availability release for Gemini 1.5 Pro's 2M context window.\nL831: \nL832: API updates:\nL833: \nL834:   * Added support for cite101†code execution .\nL835: \nL836: ## June 18, 2024\nL837: \nL838: API updates:\nL839: \nL840:   * Added support for cite135†context caching .\n"
